          ],
          "content": "**Page no. 164**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.437,
            0.421,
            0.47
          ],
          "content": "**Q1. Are the lengths** $\\frac { 1 } { 2 }$ **and** $\\frac{3}{6}$ **equal?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.478,
            0.22,
            0.495
          ],
          "content": "Ans. Yes."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.504,
            0.508,
            0.537
          ],
          "content": "Q2. $\\mathbf { A r e }   { \\frac { 2 } { 3 } }$ **and** $\\frac{4}{6}$ **equivalent fractions? Why?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.545,
            0.799,
            0.563
          ],
          "content": "Ans. Yes, since they are of equal length which can be seen in fractional wall also."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.57,
            0.615,
            0.604
          ],
          "content": "**Q3. How many pieces of length** $\\frac{1}{6}$ **will make a length of** $\\left( \\frac { 1 } { 2 } \\right) _ { \\circ } ^ { 2 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.612,
            0.237,
            0.63
          ],
          "content": "Ans. 3 pieces."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.637,
            0.615,
            0.671
          ],
          "content": "**Q4. How many pieces of length** $\\frac{1}{6}$ **will make a length of** $\\frac { 1 } { 3 } ?$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.679,
            0.255,
            0.696
          ],
          "content": "Ans. 2 pieces."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.706,
            0.233,
            0.724
          ],
          "content": "**Page no. 165**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.733,
            0.233,
            0.751
          ],
          "content": "**Figure it out**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.758,
            0.578,
            0.793
          ],
          "content": "**Q1. Are** $\\frac { 3 } { 6 } , \\frac { 4 } { 8 } ,$ **and** $\\frac { 5 } { 1 0 }$ **are equivalent fractions? Why?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.8,
            0.709,
            0.819
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** Yes. In the fraction wall their lengths can be seen to be equal."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.827,
            0.475,
            0.859
          ],
          "content": "**Q2. Write two equivalent fractions for** $\\frac{2}{6}.$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.865,
            0.852,
            0.9
          ],
          "content": "Ans. Two equivalent fractions for ${ \\frac { 2 } { 6 } } \\operatorname { a r e } { \\frac { 1 } { 3 } } \\operatorname { a n d } { \\frac { 3 } { 9 } } .$ (Try for other equivalent fractions also)"
        }
      ]
    }
